speechtext:
Thank you for your advice on this matter, Mr. Speaker. Given the fact that it has been so widely reported in today's press and will continue to be reported over the next day or two, I do not think there is any doubt that the report has been leaked. If you do find there has been a prima facie case of a breach of privilege I would at that time like to move the following motion:
Whereas the publication of the report of the Special Committee on Indian Self-Government before it has been reported to the House breaches the privileges of Members of this House;
I move that this matter be referred to the Standing Committee on Privileges and Elections for investigation to discern how and why this document was released before it had been reported to the House.
